By Wayne Scanlan
To understand where a team is headed, it helps to know where it has been.
Two years ago, almost to the day, we advocated a major rebuild of the listless Ottawa Senators hockey program.
A couple of weeks later, club owner Eugene Melnyk was in town and responded with this infamous diatribe, recorded at a news conference: ��Anybody that says we should blow up this organization should get their own bomb and go blow themselves up. OK?
